# Code generated by Claude
"""
Joint search over the object layout and the staging pose for slack at every task pose of the beaker-on-hotplate task.

    source .venv/bin/activate
    python experiments/beaker_hotplate_layout_search.py [--quick]

The left arm has to reach, holding the beaker upright in the grasp orientation of experiments/
beaker_hotplate_staging_search.py (approach axis within 45 deg of forward-and-down 45 deg, fingers opening sideways):
  a) grasp point: beaker mid-height, beaker at its place, fingers open
  b) 10 cm above the hotplate top, beaker held (fingers closed on it, 70 mm)
  c) set-down: held beaker's bottom 2 mm above the hotplate top
  d) the ready pose (above and in front of the beaker, fingers open) and the via waypoint of the arm path
Searched jointly: the object pair (beaker and hotplate slid together along the bench, hotplate on the robot's right,
spacing 20-30 cm, 5 cm from every bench edge, which fixes their y) and the staging pose (x, y, yaw) and pedestal height.

Requirements, in priority order (LAYOUT_CFG in src/task_config.py):
  1. hard: base-to-bench clearance >= 8 cm, swept clearance of the final turn >= 5 cm, >= 3 cm from other furniture,
     no contacts at any task pose (arm geoms >= 3 mm from everything; only the fingers may touch the beaker)
  2. every arm joint >= 10 deg from its limit at every task pose
  3. robustness: base perturbed by +-2 cm in x and y and +-2 deg in yaw (all 8 corners): every task pose still has an
     IK solution within the joint limits (1 deg inside), orientation constraints met, no contacts; the via path stays clear
Feasible candidates are ranked by the smallest joint-limit margin over all task poses, largest first. If no candidate
meets 2 or 3 nothing is relaxed: the best few are printed with their margins and the script stops.

Method: the arm's joint space is sampled (batch FK, verified against MuJoCo in beaker_hotplate_staging_search.py), the
usable samples are kept with their joint margin and put in a KD-tree. Screening: for every candidate (spacing x standoff
x yaw x lateral x pedestal, in the body frame, so independent of where along the bench the pair sits) the best margin among
samples within 1.5 cm of each task point. The best candidates are then placed at the pair x that gives the largest swept
clearance, and solved exactly with a vectorised damped-least-squares IK under joint bounds shrunk by the margin; the
largest feasible margin per pose is found by bisection, the solution must be collision-free in MuJoCo. Then the via
waypoint (largest-margin collision-free one) and the 8-corner robustness check.
"""

